res its own coupler color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/15/code.py:78:    - Each isolated station cluster and its matching train couplers share one unique non-stripe color; different pairs use different colors even when station sizes repeat.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/23/code.py:31:#         base 与 plug 的 profile 必须逐列互补。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/23/code.py:48:#    - 仍然只有两个前景组件、三种固定颜色，推理难点集中在“识别互补锯齿 + 判断旋转 + 验证嵌入”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/23/code.py:51:#    - 原 `shpA == shpB` 不成立：现在匹配条件是 complementary profile，而不是相同条形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/23/code.py:79:#    - 每个 sprite 恰有一个 2-row zigzag connector；base profile 与 plug profile 互补。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/23/code.py:277:    Rotate the plug back by a quarter-turn, align complementary zigzag connectors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D10/0/code.py:32:#   Each adjacent pair encodes one substitution \"source color -> target color\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/20/code.py:589:    - The combo still resolves each true pair by “coupler count picks the station, marker colors fix the orientation”, but now that logic must be applied only after filtering out the fake train and fake station and after decoding the cross-shaped divider geometry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D13/0/code.py:752:    block_patch = _make_blocking_pair_patch(winner_color, loser_color, block_shadow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/45/code.py:110:  - The duplicate pair shares a palette, so the useful information is the arrangement of colors, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/12/code.py:370:    color_pairs = _assign_color_pairs(len(placements))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/bf45cf4b/D7/1/code.py:3:# Change: 控制精灵中的空洞位置填充瓦片大小的纯背景色区域... → 空洞位置填充瓦片颜色的互补/映射版本\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/12/code.py:14:#   2. The two connectors are not identical. They are complementary T shapes living\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/12/code.py:29:# - The connector family is small on purpose: only two complementary T-pairs. This keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/12/code.py:36:#   complementary mapping from base-shape to plug-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/20270e3b/12/code.py:63:#   * base/plug connector shapes differ but are complementary;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/13/code.py:24:#      color-based pairing across obstacles and color-based direction across the two obstacle colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/27/code.py:380:def _make_duplicate_pair(slot_a: dict, slot_b: dict, k: int, color_pool: list[int]) -> tuple[dict, dict] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/27/code.py:797:    dup_pair = _make_duplicate_pair(dup_slots[0], dup_slots[1], k, piece_color_pool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/27/code.py:821:    if dup_pair[0][\"color_set\"] != dup_pair[1][\"color_set\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D9/2/code.py:860:    built = _build_object_pair(layout, colors, bg, outline_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:66:      if a flip-enabled solver swapped the pair, the output colors in those two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:744:def _gen_pair_colorings(slot_a: dict, slot_b: dict, piece_palette: list[int]) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:747:    pair_colors_a = random.sample(piece_palette, 2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:748:    remaining = [c for c in piece_palette if c not in pair_colors_a]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:749:    pair_colors_b = random.sample(remaining, 2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:751:        grid_a = _assign_block_colors(slot_a[\"mask\"], pair_colors_a)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:752:        grid_b = _assign_block_colors(slot_b[\"mask\"], pair_colors_b)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:787:    pair_colors = _gen_pair_colorings(pair_slot_a, pair_slot_b, piece_palette)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:788:    if pair_colors is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/8/code.py:790:    pair_grid_a, pair_grid_b = pair_colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:84:    - Fill holes with the paired source colors and tight-crop the result.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:509:def _assign_pair_colors(layout: list[dict], fill_pool: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:517:    if n_pairs >= n_colors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:518:        pair_colors = list(fill_pool) + [random.choice(fill_pool) for _ in range(n_pairs - n_colors)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:520:        pair_colors = list(fill_pool)[:n_pairs]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:521:    random.shuffle(pair_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:523:    pair_color_map = dict(zip(unique_pair_ids, pair_colors))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:524:    colors = [pair_color_map[slot[\"pair_id\"]] for slot in layout]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:608:def _build_object_pair(layout: list[dict], colors: list[int], bg: int, outline_col: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:671:    colors = _assign_pair_colors(layout, fill_pool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D2/0/code.py:673:    built = _build_object_pair(layout, colors, bg, outline_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/19/code.py:20:#      pairing is visible without exploding the color vocabulary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/21/code.py:22:#     paired source colors in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/21/code.py:40:#     explicit source->target pairs from the legend and cannot infer them from non-bg colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/21/code.py:143:    Read a top legend with two source->target pairs, then apply bidirectional color swaps around same-color '+' motifs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/21/code.py:147:    - Rows 0..1 contain exactly two vertical legend pairs, each giving one source color above its target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/21/code.py:152:    - For each mapping independently, any playfield pixel already in that mapping's target color swaps back to the paired source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/21/code.py:153:    - Also for each mapping independently, any source-colored pixel whose 4 orthogonal neighbors are the same source color defines a '+' footprint; recolor that 5-cell footprint to the paired target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/21/code.py:156:    Key insight: The legend controls both directions of each color pair. Target-colored input pixels are not a second motif family to detect; they are reverse-swap evidence, while '+' detection still runs only on the untouched source-color layers in the playfield.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/24/code.py:381:    - Bounding boxes are no longer sufficient: the puzzle is solved by exact mask coverage. The distinctive extra step is to detect when two smaller outside fragments are complementary parts of one larger cavity and must be assembled before filling it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/4/code.py:10:#    pairing, while each station also carries one repeated-color indicator pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/4/code.py:40:#    colors are unique per pair and are limited by the color budget. This keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/4/code.py:178:    Key insight: pairing and orientation are both decided at the destination. The label color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/14/code.py:265:    ccw, cw = _orth_pair(color_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/14/code.py:273:        ccw, cw = _orth_pair(color_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/14/code.py:509:        ccw, cw = _orth_pair(color_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e4f6532/14/code.py:1244:                    ccw, cw = _orth_pair(dirs[color])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:276:        assert target_key not in pairs, \"each active target must have exactly one connector color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:277:        pairs[target_key] = int(color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/26/code.py:280:    return pairs, connector_colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/0/code.py:14:#      The marker colors are the pairing key. The fill color of the `src` cavity is still what\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/3/code.py:384:    color_pairs = _assign_color_pairs(len(rects), bg, base, marker)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/1/code.py:553:    built = _build_object_pair(layout, prototypes, colors_by_shape, bg, outline_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:605:def _assign_pair_colors(layout: list[dict], fill_pool: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:613:    if n_pairs >= n_colors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:614:        pair_colors = list(fill_pool) + [random.choice(fill_pool) for _ in range(n_pairs - n_colors)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:616:        pair_colors = list(fill_pool)[:n_pairs]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:617:    random.shuffle(pair_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:619:    pair_color_map = dict(zip(unique_pair_ids, pair_colors))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:620:    colors = [pair_color_map[slot[\"pair_id\"]] for slot in layout]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:728:    colors = _assign_pair_colors(layout, fill_pool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D1/3/code.py:730:    built = _build_object_pair(layout, colors, bg, outline_col)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/17/code.py:58:  detect the structural color pair by scanning non-bg pairs for large disconnected components that contain both colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/17/code.py:89:- The structural pair never appears as normal fill colors elsewhere, so the marker reads as a deliberate cue instead\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/17/code.py:242:    Fill several separated bichromatic frames by first finding the structural color pair, then routing each sprite to its frame and color-tagged hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/800d221b/7/code.py:269:    - Recolor each physical branch together with its local seed border to the paired seed's original majority color, then swap that seed interior's majority/minority colors in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:27:# - 原题：外部碎片是按 k 放大的洞形；solver 通过“最小实心正方形碎片的边长”读出 k，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:28:#   然后把每个碎片按 k*k 块降采样，与框架内部洞形做 D4 匹配。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:30:#   实心正方形，因此“最小正方形碎片”这条捷径被彻底切断。取而代之，框架边框上嵌入一圈\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:32:# - 具体例子：若某例有 4 个槽洞，外面散落 4 个彩色碎片；框架左、右两边各能看到 6 个和\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:34:#   再仅统计其边框四边上的非框架色像素数，恢复 k=2；之后仍按块级形状匹配碎片与洞。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:35:# - 差异：原题在“几何块大小 -> k”这一步依赖外部碎片；融合版在这一步依赖边框数字编码，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:36:#   且生成器专门避免让碎片重新泄露 k。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:43:#   外部碎片就会太乱，若自由度过低，又会和单变体样例太像。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:47:#   但面积远大于任一碎片或干扰点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:50:# - 原代码“扫描最小实心正方形碎片读 k”的前提被明确打破：没有 unit 槽，也禁止实心方块槽。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:52:# - `pieces = non-singleton components excluding frame` 仍成立：标记附着在框架上，不会被分离成碎片。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:53:# - `downsample_blocks` 现在依赖边框解出的 k；生成器保证所有碎片确实由 2x2 实心块拼接，因此\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:59:# - 洞区之间依旧 8 分离；外部碎片用 `random_free_location(..., padding=1, padding_connectivity=8)`\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:61:# - 干扰物仍是孤立单像素，颜色独立，不会误并入碎片组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:65:# - 输出始终是 2 倍放大后的框架；由于没有 unit 洞或小实心方块碎片，最直接的尺度线索只剩边框编码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:69:# - 标记只占据最外层边框；洞、墙、碎片、干扰点各自处于不同空间层级，没有区域叠加。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:70:# - 每个碎片单色、每个非 unit 槽形 D4 唯一，避免出现大量同色同形干扰。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:71:# - 输出图不保留标记，只保留放大后的框架和填入后的碎片，延续原题简洁外观。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:74:# - 本融合不引入颜色映射；颜色只承担“框架 / 标记 / 碎片 / 干扰”角色，推理重点是数量编码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:76:# - 变化主要来自槽洞布局与碎片朝向，而不是颜色规则，因此 2-3 组样例就足以归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/39/code.py:83:# - 假设没有任何碎片能通过“自身是实心正方形”把 k 再泄露出来：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/53/code.py:46:    - Combo: read the scale square to get k=2 -> read the color-pair legend -> detect colored slots\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/53/code.py:87:    - The repeated-shape pair ensures that ignoring the color legend changes the placement logic.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/53/code.py:215:    - The top-left corner is a 2-column color legend: each row pairs a slot-marker color with a sprite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/8/code.py:48:#       - \"align using red pixels\" is invalid because each pair aligns on its own anchor color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/8/code.py:77:#     - Color equality is the pairing cue; size only affects scaling once the color-selected source is known.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/8/code.py:458:            int(pair[\"color\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/8/code.py:480:            int(pair[\"color\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/14/code.py:60:#      The color change is tied to a structural repair event, not to absolute color values.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/20/code.py:33:  - The generator forces at least one duplicate non-unit shape pair, so color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/800d221b/35/code.py:12:#   A fully general \"unique pair per seed\" setup would exceed the 10-color ARC palette once seed count reaches 4,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/800d221b/35/code.py:26:#   The three seed pairs are pairwise disjoint, frames all share P1, and only branches recolor, so a human can spot:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/20/code.py:446:    color_pairs = _choose_color_pairs(bg, base, marker, count)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D3/0/code.py:430:COLOR_MISMATCH_RATE = 0.10             # P(cavity breaks mirror-pair color sharing)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D3/0/code.py:683:def _assign_pair_colors(layout: list[dict], fill_pool: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D3/0/code.py:691:    if n_pairs >= n_colors:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3a25b0d8/D3/0/code.py: