 marker bracketing still fall back to the smaller color id.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/0/code.py:891:        crossing_pairs[pt] = colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/0/code.py:956:            forced = {color for color in crossing_pairs[pt] if pt in yellow_rays.get(color, set())}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/2/code.py:162:    Reassign the outside sprites by nearest frame row, then show the complementary tally inside each frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/2/code.py:176:    - The displayed dot count is the complement of the true count, so more nearby sprites produce fewer dots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/5/code.py:214:    - A separate two-row legend on the wallpaper pairs each sprite's dominant body color with a different marker code color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/5/code.py:447:    pairs = list(zip(body_colors, code_colors))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:3:# Change: 黄色控制射线优先；否则原始交叉处选碎片度更高的颜色（pre-repair连通分量更多者胜出），纯填充交叉选较小颜色ID... → 交叉处选线段更长的颜色\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:10:#    The only semantic change is what happens when two repaired colors both claim one crossing cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:31:#      straight run through the candidate crossing cell inside each repaired color mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:151:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by restoring singleton markers, filling straight gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/16/code.py:20:#     opposite side of the same anchor. The fused lobe is the pair's color template masked by the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/16/code.py:254:    - For each diagonal pair, take the top patch as a shape mask and the bottom patch as a color template. Keep the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:313:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line tree by recoloring singleton markers, filling orthogonal gaps, and rotating yellow-marked arms without destroying same-color branches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:325:    - At overlap cells, yellow rays win; otherwise choose the most visibly supported repaired claimant, prioritizing fragmentation and marker bracketing rather than color id.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:327:    Key insight: The singleton markers are still local repair cues, but once same-color junctions are allowed the decisive evidence is no longer \"which path endpoint is closest\" alone; the correct color is the one whose surrounding visible arms assemble the intended tree hub or redirected branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D1/3/code.py:21:# - The original task paired a sprite to a bar through color identity:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D1/3/code.py:166:    - Order sprites by total area from large to small.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/1/code.py:101:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by replacing singleton markers, filling orthogonal gaps, and clipping yellow-marked arms at the marker cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/2/code.py:102:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by restoring singleton markers, filling ordinary orthogonal gaps, and rotating yellow-controlled gaps by copying a perpendicular arm length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/2/code.py:114:    - At overlaps, yellow-reflected spans win; otherwise an original-vs-filled crossing uses the more fragmented pre-repair line color, while pure filled crossings use the lower color id.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/27/code.py:126:    - For each rank pair, place that source color stack immediately above the matched projection's top, truncating only if the available space is shorter than the stack.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/27/code.py:311:        slot_pairs = [(int(count), int(col), int(color)) for col, count, color in zip(slot_cols, counts, colors)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:51:#       - solver repairs the pink pixel as color B, then follows that straight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:195:    Repair a thin colored line network by recoloring singleton repair markers, filling rectilinear gaps, redirecting yellow-controlled arms, and honoring pink crossing priorities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:207:    Key insight: The singleton symbols still identify how sparse fragments should be repaired, but the pink symbol adds a third instruction channel: after the repaired geometry is reconstructed, that marker points along its straight run to the crossing where its color must stay visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:259:    repair_marker_pts = {color: set() for color in line_colors}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:265:        repair_marker_pts[color].add(pt)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:272:        return (r, c) in repair_marker_pts[color] or _axis_support(masks[color], r, c, axis)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:290:        if (r1, c1) in repair_marker_pts[color] and (r2, c2) in repair_marker_pts[color]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:342:                    repair_marker_pts[color].discard(q)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:372:        same_row = [mc for mr, mc in repair_marker_pts[color] if mr == r]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:375:        same_col = [mr for mr, mc in repair_marker_pts[color] if mc == c]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:138:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network whose instructions are encoded as two-cell red/yellow domino markers instead of singleton pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:150:    - At crossings, yellow-control rays win; otherwise an original-vs-filled crossing uses the more fragmented pre-repair line color, while pure filled crossings use the lower color id.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/29/code.py:399:    pairs = _choose_rule_colors(num_rules)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:75:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by reinterpreting one shared marker color as either a missing bend cell or an arm-side redirection control.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:88:    - At crossings, control-ray cells win; otherwise an original-vs-filled crossing uses the more fragmented pre-repair line color, while pure filled crossings use the lower color id.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:3:# Name: 轮廓互补匹配+向下凸起\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:16:#      2) colors no longer stay in the same absolute column, but instead follow a complementary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:19:#      the complementary levels must realize the four distinct values {1,2,3,4}; with outer columns\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:26:#    - The generator uses a permutation of tooth heights [1,2,3,4], so the complementary free-space\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:51:#      teeth point downward, and the colored-height profile in the input is a permuted complement of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:53:#      the tooth with matching complementary clearance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:62:#      input columns with unique heights 1..4, and a unique complementary match from heights to spaces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:83:    Insert a downward-toothed grey bar into a top-open grey frame by complementary contour match, then hang each color stack below its matched tooth.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/11/code.py:94:    Key insight: The decisive relation is a complementary contour in the downward direction: deeper teeth leave shorter hanging space, shallower teeth leave taller hanging space, and colors follow that lock-and-key fit rather than their original x-position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:26:#      template bbox, it draws the complement of the template in O, leaving the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:46:#   turns are visible; the template is also non-full, so the origin complement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:57:#   That assumption is broken: the origin support is the bbox complement, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:62:# - Rendering the complement after the positive copies is safe only if stamp\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:92:#   becomes the origin-complement foreground in the output. No hidden ordering\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:130:def _complement_cells(cells: list[tuple[int, int]], size: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:131:    \"\"\"Return the bbox-level complement of a shape inside a square box.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:176:def _paint_origin_complement(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:185:    \"\"\"Overwrite the origin box with the complement of the canonical template.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:204:    \"\"\"Render the fused rule: quadrant-rotated positives plus an origin complement.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:220:    _paint_origin_complement(out, bg, overlap_col, base_r, base_c, size, templ_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:236:    \"\"\"Single-variant baseline: unrotated positives plus an origin complement.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:252:    _paint_origin_complement(out, bg, overlap_col, base_r, base_c, size, templ_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:298:    - The origin does not receive a normal template copy. Instead, inside the template bbox draw the complement of the canonical template in color O, leaving template cells as background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:438:def _is_complement_distinct(cells: list[tuple[int, int]], size: int) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:439:    \"\"\"Reject templates whose complement matches a positive rotation exactly.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:440:    comp = frozenset(_complement_cells(cells, size))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:445:    \"\"\"Square, spanning, rotationally asymmetric template with a visible complement.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/16/code.py:453:        if not _is_complement_distinct(cells, size):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/43/code.py:64:#     4-neighbors of the legend pair, which avoids bogus colored pairs near the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/898e7135/D3/2/code.py:32:    pairing_rule: color -> position mapping, not shape -> position mapping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/0/code.py:424:    Repair a sparse one-cell-thick line network by recoloring singleton markers, filling orthogonal gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked arms until they hit an obstacle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:23:#   the origin copy is not a recolored positive stamp. It is the complement of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:34:#     paints only the 2 complement cells in O and turns the former 7 template cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:44:#   below 100%, so every origin bbox contains a non-empty complement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:56:#   now uses different support: the template complement, not the template cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:77:#   complement cue are local, repeated, and independent of absolute color ids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:89:#   template, so the complement-origin output always differs from a recolored origin.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:96:# - main() assumes the template bbox is not full so that the complement is non-empty;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:137:    - At the origin offset, draw the template's complement inside the bbox: former template cells become bg and former bbox-empty cells become O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:256:    \"\"\"Generate a 4-connected spanning template whose bbox complement is non-empty.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/9/code.py:395:    \"\"\"Build one combo instance with a nearest-point origin and complement-rendered self copy.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/9/code.py:125:    - A tiny 2-row legend in the top-left corner pairs each sprite's dominant body color (top row) with the destination code color that refers to it (bottom row).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/26/code.py:28:#    - U-pairs and two-color alternators are removed from generation for this combo. Keeping them\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:90:    Repair sparse one-cell-wide colored polylines by recoloring singleton markers, bridging axial gaps, and bending yellow-controlled endpoints to an edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/1/code.py:101:    - At overlaps, yellow-generated rays win; otherwise original crossings still prefer the more fragmented pre-repair color, with the same tie-breaks as the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/25/code.py:5:# Name: 碎片对称聚合补全\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/25/code.py:18:#    - 为了让 D11 和 D13 都明显可见，generator 固定使用 3 个局部组：左/中/右三个竖轴对称碎片。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/25/code.py:25:#      这个假设在 D13/1 下会失效，因为输入里允许出现同色旁观碎片；它们不该被补全。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/25/code.py:30:#      但 generator 不依赖它，避免和“多碎片聚合”的主视觉冲突。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/25/code.py:44:#    - 没有颜色映射。颜色只承担“把某个局部碎片与它自己的红轴对应起来”的作用。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/45/code.py:721:    found_pairs = {(int(rule[\"source_color\"]), int(rule[\"target_color\"])) for rule in discovered}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:29:#       - 仍保留 2-4 条线色、交叉、碎片度裁决与黄色翻臂, 所以任务没有被简化成单一路径修补\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:35:#       - crossing disambiguation: 依赖 comp_count 是“输入修补前, 但把 marker 视作其所属线色后”的碎片数; 新 generator 继续维护这一点\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:143:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by recoloring singleton markers, filling rectilinear gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked arms using the farthest visible line color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:155:    - At overlaps, yellow-control rays override everything else; otherwise crossings are resolved by pre-repair fragmentation, with lower color id breaking ties among equally filled claims.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/8/code.py:210:    - Same-color controls form solid L paths or full-span stripes; one optional pair of singleton colors forms one alternating-color L path whose endpoint colors fix the phase.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:31:#   origin uses the template's bbox-level complement. Every local bg cell in the bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:47:# - To keep the complement visually legible, the generator only uses holey templates\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:48:#   whose bbox complement has at least 3 cells. This avoids tiny 1-2 pixel negatives\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:61:#   origin complement afterwards.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:65:#   it uses only filled pixels, while the origin complement must use the full bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:66:#   complement. That is the key interaction between D3 and D8+D11.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:72:#   the complement origin, and the hole signal visually separable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:83:#   O marks non-origin lattice points and reappears as the origin-complement color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:240:        if is_origin and origin_mode == \"complement\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:260:    assert origin_mode == \"complement\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:274:    Replicate a holey template from a singleton lattice, but place every copy by centroid alignment and render the origin as a complement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:285:    - Non-origin lattice points stamp the template's filled mask in T. The origin point instead stamps the bbox-level complement of the template in O, and any overlap among positive stamps is also O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:290:    return _solve_with_modes(grid, anchor_mode=\"centroid\", origin_mode=\"complement\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:367:        complement_area = int(total - area)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/4/code.py:370:        if complement_area < MIN_COMPLEMENT_A