e.py:464:    pair_color = avail.pop()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/7/code.py:465:    objs[pair_shared][\"color\"] = pair_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/7/code.py:466:    objs[pair_unique][\"color\"] = pair_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/7/code.py:555:    noise = _add_noise_pixels(inp, bg, [pair_color] + avail)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/3/code.py:24:#      5. 为避免 D8/2 退化成“旋转了但结果没变”，远端输出改成带方向 tip 的互补形状：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/3/code.py:79:# Base orientations for the transported, rotation-sensitive complements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/3/code.py:334:    Route each token through an empty maze and rotate its delivered complement at 9-gates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/3/code.py:342:    - Solid sources collapse in place to diamonds. At the far site, the placeholder is replaced by the source's complementary shape with a directional tip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D4/2/code.py:45:# - Each canonical hole shape appears multiple times and is paired with several sprite colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/26/code.py:69:#   Only one lane disappears and only one color pair duplicates. Visible sprite colors are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/26/code.py:335:    lane_colors[dup_pair[0]] = dup_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/26/code.py:336:    lane_colors[dup_pair[1]] = dup_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/26/code.py:345:    dup_count = sum(1 for pair in combinations(visible, 2) if lane_colors[pair[0]] == lane_colors[pair[1]])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/22/code.py:97:   - Equal pair counts and unique colors make the correspondence legible from few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/11/code.py:33:#   complementary shape is copied to every reachable leaf, not just one far endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/11/code.py:285:    - The original shape-complement rule still applies, but routing is no longer a permutation. The maroon square\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/41/code.py:23:#      3. pair the i-th ordered frame with the i-th ordered solid and swap their colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/41/code.py:29:#      After paired color swap by ordered index:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:85:    Choose the pair of non-bg colors whose union forms the repeated plus components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:253:    - Recover the repeated plus footprint by detecting the pair of colors whose union forms the large symmetric anchor components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D15/2/code.py:265:    plus_pair = detect_plus_color_pair(g, bg=bg, min_h=3, min_w=3, connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/10/code.py:675:        discovered_pairs = {(int(rule[\"source_color\"]), int(rule[\"target_color\"])) for rule in discovered}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/20/code.py:75:#    - Colors are only a separator aid. One pair reuses a color on purpose to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/20/code.py:392:    pair_color = int(palette[0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/20/code.py:397:            obj[\"color\"] = pair_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/62593bfd/20/code.py:520:    pair_shared, pair_unique, palette = _assign_colors(objs, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:8:#      then rewrote that token into diamond/X complements across the routed endpoint pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:14:#      complementary L-pair borrowed from D4/3:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:16:#        * a 4-cell complementary heavy L fragment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:21:#      stamps the rotated 4-cell complement at the far endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:23:#      4-cell local fragment on the source side and sends the 5-cell complement to the wire-matched top endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:50:#      squares or Xs, and outputs contain two irregular L fragments rather than diamond/X complements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:285:    Route L/T-shaped source tokens through the original wire permutation, but resolve each source into a family-dependent pair of complementary L-fragments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:292:    - Replace each L-source in place with the 5-cell heavy-L half and transmit its 4-cell complementary heavy-L half to the endpoint reached by following that wire component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/7/code.py:293:    - Replace each T-source in place with the 4-cell heavy-L half and transmit the 5-cell complementary heavy-L half instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/21/code.py:74:#       accidental extra pairings or ambiguous color stories.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/24/code.py:237:    - Each source lane turns grey (5), and its sprite count is recreated in the paired target lane using the target lane's existing color, stacked into empty slots from the bottom upward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/24/code.py:347:        out, source_idxs, target_idxs, pairs, output_counts = _build_output(input_counts, lane_colors, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/17/code.py:367:    Route complementary tokens and reveal a segment-indexed dashed travel trail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/19/code.py:277:    Learn paired same-color legends, then use global source-color frequency to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/15/code.py:340:    Route colored 3x3 tokens through a mostly unmarked wire network and rebuild the complementary token at the far endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/11/code.py:197:    Pair red and green lanes globally, then perform per-pair color swaps plus transfers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/11/code.py:205:    - Inside each matched pair, the source lane keeps its sprite count in place but recolors to the target lane's input color; the target lane's pre-existing sprites recolor to the source lane's input color; and copied source sprites fill higher empty slots in the target lane using the target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:8:#    - 基础题里，token 变形规则不复杂，关键是沿青色网络把“互补形”送到另一端。原 solver 在交叉处几乎总能靠\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:364:    - The token-shape transformation is still the original complementary solid/X/diamond cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/2/code.py:365:    - The new challenge is two-layer routing: arrows define the default local turn map, but blue crossings visibly override that default. Correct endpoint pairing therefore depends on learning both the arrow family and the color priority.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D14/0/code.py:44:  longer holds, so frame detection must search over pairs of colors and use their union mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D14/0/code.py:80:- The solver assumes the true frame pair forms the largest valid two-color connected component whose bbox\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D14/0/code.py:174:    solver must first infer the frame color pair and keep that pattern unchanged while only recoloring the holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D14/0/code.py:179:    # STEP 1) Find the patterned frame as the largest valid component formed by a pair of colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/16/code.py:511:    - A complementary remote shape is added only if the token truly reaches another original endpoint on the remaining pipe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/25/code.py:80:# - This inference uses only visible structure and repeated color pairs, not color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/25/code.py:541:    - Activation keeps the blob body's boundary in its original body color, recolors only the body's interior to that body's paired active color, and then emits a thick red ray through the green port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/9/code.py:33:- Original branch “emit complementary X/diamond” is invalid and must be replaced by one uniform\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/18/code.py:7:#    Original a25697e4 pairs a tool to a frame by a color-region area equal to one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:15:# - 原题里，每个顶/底端点外侧放一个 token；solid 会在原位裂成 diamond，并把互补的 X 送到线路另一端，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:18:#   过滤器若面积为偶数，token 可以穿过；若面积为奇数，token 在此被拦下，不再向远端发送互补形状。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:20:#   但只有通过偶面积过滤器的那些 token 才会真的在底部出现互补形状。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:27:#   3. 差异：输出底部只缺失 A 的互补形状，而且这个缺失并不是“没有线路”，而是“线路存在但被奇面积 9 块阻断”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:37:#   否则 solver 会错误地给被阻断的 token 生成远端互补形状。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:52:# - 单一 cycle 通过整条线路拓扑可见；过滤规则通过“同样有线路，但有些底部位置始终不出现互补形状”可见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:263:    - A token also tries to send its complementary shape to the far endpoint determined by the wire permutation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/10/code.py:265:      so no remote complementary shape is created.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/21/code.py:11:      - the remote outputs are still complementary fragments derived from a solid source\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/19/code.py:16:#   endpoint. The new stop rule no longer targets the far endpoint: the emitted complementary token is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/19/code.py:31:#   shorter/longer travel distance of the emitted complement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/19/code.py:227:    Convert each source token in place, then send its complement partway along the connected pipe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/19/code.py:238:    - The emitted complement does not go to the far endpoint. Instead it stops on the traced wire after a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d59b0160/D5/3/code.py:145:    - For each other connected component, test every legend pair and ask whether those two colors ever touch by a 4-neighbor edge inside that component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d59b0160/D5/3/code.py:154:    assert legend_pairs, \"legend contains no color pairs\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d59b0160/D5/3/code.py:374:    roles = [\"delete_all_pairs\"] * deleted_count + [\"keep_broken_all_colors\", \"keep_partial\", \"keep_partial\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:7:#    Original a25697e4 pairs each movable 2-color tool to a border frame by the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/27/code.py:70:#    component, and each pair uses only three colors. No legends, hidden numeric\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:15:# - 保留原题的 token 语义：solid 3x3 会在原地裂解为 diamond；solid/X 都会把互补形状送到管道另一端。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:263:    Route colored tokens through a dense orthogonal/diagonal lattice and emit their complementary 3x3 patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/4/code.py:273:    - Any solid or X token at one endpoint sends its complementary shape to the far endpoint reached by tracing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/8/code.py:33:#   Each pair uses four distinct non-background colors: bar, notch, plug, handle. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/20/code.py:59:#     - Lane colors remain pairwise distinct, which avoids same-color touching sprites across adjacent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/24/code.py:442:    - Sort the tools by total area from large to small and dock them into the chamber from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:27:#      sends the missing diamond-part back. Because both endpoints already contain the complementary stationary half,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:49:#    - Original routing rewrote only the source side locally and only wrote one far-side complement. That assumption is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:78:#    - For each top endpoint, tracing the wire reaches one bottom endpoint with the same token color and the complementary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:277:    Complete both ends of every routed channel by mutually exchanging complementary token halves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:286:    - Diamond and X are complementary halves of a solid 3x3 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:289:    - At each far endpoint, the arriving complement is overlaid onto the already-present partial, so both endpoint\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:294:      hold complementary same-colored partials, and then complete both sides of the channel rather than only one side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/28/code.py:570:    \"\"\"Place complementary partial pairs on both ends and solid outputs on both ends.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/1/code.py:20:#      fallback would cross-pair them. This keeps the D1 color-pairing change active.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/1/code.py:143:def _build_left_pair(bg: int, frame_color: int, handle_color: int):\n/h