et.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/14/code.py:498:    - Find the training pair by matching non-zero color sets rather than by frame size or position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/30/code.py:205:    - The dominant color is the background. One repeated non-background color marks endpoint pairs that sit on 45-degree diagonals, while differently colored pixels on those same diagonals are the ray triggers. Extra off-diagonal distractors may also appear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/2/code.py:3:# Change: 形状补全（shape_completion）——如果管道一端已存在十字形或四角星形，则在另一端放置互补形状（四角星对应十字，十字对应四角星），颜色与已有形状相同 → 镜像翻转补全\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/2/code.py:9:#    - Replace the symmetric diamond/X pair with an asymmetric complementary pair inside the same 3x3 window:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/2/code.py:13:#    - The D5 change is applied only to the emitted complementary shape: before stamping CORE at the far end,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/2/code.py:25:#    - The complementary pair is intentionally asymmetric; otherwise the mirror step would be invisible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/2/code.py:293:    - A solid token or an existing ANCHOR token emits the complementary CORE block to the opposite endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D5/2/code.py:294:    - Before placing that complementary CORE block, mirror it according to the whole wire component:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/19/code.py:319:        pair = [int(color) for color in region_pairs[i]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/29/code.py:328:    - `paired_colors`: mover colors with at least two row marks and two column marks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/29/code.py:351:    paired_colors = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/29/code.py:357:            paired_colors += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/29/cod