adab01/12/code.py:267:    - A top+left pair or a bottom+right pair of the same marker color encodes one glyph top-left coordinate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/12/code.py:271:    - Reconstruct each placement from its edge pair, then map the marker color to the same fixed glyph alphabet as the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/12/code.py:448:        assert stats[\"real_pairs\"] == sum(1 for _color, _channel, _r0, _c0, is_legend in placements if not is_legend)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:31:#      members of one opposite-edge pair, and at least one sprite of that color lands on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:316:    - Each marker color has an opposite-edge border-anchor pair, and one color may have extra same-color anchors on the perpendicular border pair as well.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:710:    contest_pair = _pair_for_axis(out, bg, contest_axis, contest_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:742:            pair = _pair_for_axis(out, bg, axis, color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:845:        \"pair_split_colors\": 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:868:            profile[\"pair_split_colors\"] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/17/code.py:883:    return bool(profile[\"contest_colors\"] and profile[\"axis_split_colors\"] and profile[\"pair_split_colors\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/25/code.py:323:    Stamp frame-selected patterned sprites into a framed region using outside sprite templates and paired multicolor legends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/19/code.py:325:    Key insight: The legends now control two things at once: recoloring still comes from each source->target pair, but equal target colors must be merged into the same output panel across all frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:61:#    pair, and parity decides whether a marker keeps its own row's left color or flips to its pair\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:74:#   - main() assumes row pairing is recovered by vertical proximity rather than by numeric color ids;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/0/code.py:8:#   complementary token appears at the other end of the same wire. The change is only in how channel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/0/code.py:230:    - A solid 3x3 token collapses in place into a diamond, and its complementary X-pattern is sent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/26/code.py:612:    slot_to_color: dict[tuple[int, int], int] = {special_pair[0]: special_color, special_pair[1]: special_color}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/2/code.py:57:#   Colors only encode anchor-marker pairing. No ordering over color ids is used. The visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/2/code.py:259:    - Isolated border singletons act as anchors, and a sprite is paired to the anchor with the same marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/49/code.py:3:# Name: 碎片紧密排列+干扰像素\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/49/code.py:9:#       - 输出仍是把真实碎片拼成一个严格左右镜像的致密矩形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/49/code.py:12:#       - 非框架碎片不再随机散开，而是被压进一个紧凑托盘，piece bbox 之间只有 1 像素背景缝。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/49/code.py:13:#       - 额外加入 1-3 个孤立干扰像素，专门落在这些狭窄缝隙里，颜色复用真实碎片颜色池。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/49/code.py:19:#         其余真实碎片在框架外组成一个紧凑排布区，左右或上下不重叠，piece bbox 之间恰有 1 格背景带。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/49/code.py:130:    assert len(vertical_line_candidates) <= 1, \"paired vertical edge-line color must be unique when present\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:266:    Resolve straight-through wire channels by splitting solids locally and emitting complements to the opposite endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D10/2/code.py:276:    - Unlike the crossed-routing source task, channels do not permute columns here; the only nontrivial work is recognizing the token shape and carrying its complementary shape straight across the channel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D14/0/code.py:692:    \"\"\"Choose an ordered orthogonal pair: color-coded dir + position-coded dir.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D8/2/code.py:850:def _build_pair_grids(n: int, colors: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88bcf3b4/D8/2/code.py:976:    built = _build_pair_grids(n, colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/29/code.py:170:    assert len(vertical_line_candidates) <= 1, \"paired vertical edge-line color must be unique when present\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/29/code.py:382:    - Optional corner markers, horizontal edge bars, and paired vertical edge lines are still encoded with the fragments' native colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/28/code.py:394:def _row_assignment(pattern: tuple[int, int, int, int], pair_colors: tuple[int, int], iso_color: int) -> dict[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/28/code.py:397:        return {0: pair_colors[0], 1: pair_colors[1], 3: iso_color}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/28/code.py:399:    return {0: iso_color, 2: pair_colors[0], 3: pair_colors[1]}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/28/code.py:424:        pair_colors, iso_color = schemes[rr % len(schemes)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/28/code.py:425:        for cc, col in _row_assignment(pattern, pair_colors, iso_color).items():\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/0/code.py:49:#     - 在 solid/X 分支中写入远端形状时，默认目标 3x3 区域为空或仅含互补预置 diamond；generator 保证不发生错误覆盖\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/0/code.py:247:    Move colored side tokens through a left-to-right wire layout, replacing each with its complementary 3x3 form.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/0/code.py:254:    - Every token attached to an endpoint sends its complementary pattern across the wire to the far endpoint: solid produces X, while X produces diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/0/code.py:9:#   column is a visible pair: row 0 stores a sprite border color, row 1 stores the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/0/code.py:190:    - The top edge contains a 2-row legend strip: each legend column pairs a sprite border color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/1/code.py:257:    Route edge tokens through an orthogonal wire network and materialize each token's complementary shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/1/code.py:265:    - Any endpoint token also sends its complementary pattern to the far end of the same routed wire: solid sends X, X sends diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:21:#    complementary key `3 - actual_holes`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:136:    \"\"\"Convert an actual hole count in 0..3 into its complementary lookup key.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:152:    complementary-match target value from isolated same-color dots nearby.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:203:    Recolor grey shapes by matching the complement of their hole count to a dot-coded color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:213:      that count with the 0..3 complement rule `3 - holes`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:214:    - Recolor the grey sprite to the legend color whose dot count matches that complementary value;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/37/code.py:215:      erase grey distractors whose complementary value is absent from the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/31/code.py:22:#         1) D1/0: 不再按颜色配边，而是看 hub 边缘凹口与 sprite 轮廓是否互补。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/3/code.py:257:    - Every solid 3x3 token collapses in place into a diamond, and every endpoint token sends its complementary pattern across the wire to the opposite endpoint: solid produces X, X produces diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:18:#    - The new output is a gallery: after repairing the board, isolate each color layer, tight-crop that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:165:    Convert a repaired board into a frame-separated gallery of tight-cropped color layers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:174:    assert colors, \"expected the repaired board to contain foreground colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:191:    Repair a square board from outside cue sprites, then display its color layers as separate frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:206:    itself; it is a frame-separated decomposition of that repaired board into its three nested color layers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:237:    # --- STEP 3) Separate the repaired board into one cropped frame per color layer. ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D10/1/code.py:29:#   then assigns each train/station pair a distinct leftover color from 0..7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/27/code.py:20:      2) hub 内侧四边各有一个可见的接收槽模式，精灵要靠轮廓互补去找边；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/2/code.py:27:#       - the far endpoint still receives the complementary pattern (solid -> X, X -> diamond).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/2/code.py:243:    Route endpoint tokens through an unevenly spaced wire bundle and stamp their complementary forms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/2/code.py:252:    - Any token adjacent to an endpoint sends its complementary pattern to the wire's opposite endpoint:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D11/2/code.py:259:      trace the connected wire to the far endpoint, and stamp the complementary 3x3 footprint there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:650:def _place_sprite_pairs(out_base, inp, anchors, marker_colors, bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/4/code.py:723:    placed_sprites = _place_sprite_pairs(out_base, inp, anchors, marker_colors, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/26/code.py:21:#      them are the true complementary cavities. The scattered pieces are those cavities cut out as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/26/code.py:57:#      pieces, and at least some mirrored pairs have different orientations, so \"shape complement\" is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/26/code.py:192:    - The preserved multi-part scaffold already exposes where every missing piece belongs; solving comes from complementary cavity matching across several equal-status frame fragments, not from searching for edge-aligned placements inside the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/3/code.py:22:#      the paired opposite-edge color strip as the recolor target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/3/code.py:382:      one shared ink color, while the paired bottom or right fragments show only the target recolor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/3/code.py:390:      paired opposite-edge target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/45/code.py:3:# Name: 无颜色相邻约束+仅两个大碎片\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/45/code.py:31:#    - exactly one translated pair tiles the rectangle and yields LR color symmetry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/45/code.py:136:    - Color adjacency is no longer a safe separator. The reliable cue is the long complementary seam between the two large pieces, with symmetry used only to choose the one translation pair that closes the rectangle correctly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D7/2/code.py:11:#     - 2-4 monochrome sprites are still paired to hub sides by color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/11/code.py:255:        assert score_pairs[0][0] < score_pairs[1][0], f\"ambiguous nearest target for color {color_entries[0]['color']}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/0/code.py:3:# Change: 管道对端端点（pipeline far endpoint）——token的互补形状传输到同一管道的另一端点，距端点2格处... → 距离编码停止\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/0/code.py:19:#   - the complementary token no longer goes to the far main endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/0/code.py:292:    - Each active token emits its complementary shape, but the destination is chosen by distance: count the token's colored cells (solid=9, X=5), walk that many wire steps from the source endpoint, then place the emitted shape at the side spur attached there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/30/code.py:39:#    - For every placeholder color there is exactly one non-legend diagonal-marker pair of that color outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/30/code.py:245:def _diagonal_pair_patch(h: int, w: int, color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/47/code.py:3:# Name: 部分碎片需旋转+连接器匹配\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:3:# Change: 管道对端端点（pipeline far endpoint）——token的互补形状传输到同一管道的另一端点，距端点2格处放置... → 碰撞停止\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:13:      - The complementary token always appears at the opposite endpoint, with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:19:      - A transmitted complement first tries the outer slot. If that slot is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:21:        complement, it stops in the inner slot instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:27:        empty. Under the old rule the complement appears at the single fixed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:30:        diamond, the old rule would still write the complement at the far slot,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:31:        while the variant leaves the blocker in place and stops the complement\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:48:      can depend on previously placed complements, this variant sorts connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:62:      diamond on the other; this gives a visible reason why some complements\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:473:    Route token complements through the wire network, but stop early when the far slot is already occupied.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:481:    - The complementary shape travels to the routed opposite endpoint and tries to occupy the outer landing slot first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:482:    - If that outer slot already contains another token or an earlier emitted complement, the moving shape stops in the inner slot instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/1/code.py:485:    - D7 no longer means \"always write the complement at one fixed far endpoint position\"; the visible output depends on whether the far landing slot is free or blocked.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/31/code.py:3:# Name: 按行排列+碎片按列分组\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/2/code.py:3:# Change: 管道对端端点（pipeline far endpoint）——token的互补形状传输到同一管道的另一端点，距端点2格处... → 堆叠式放置\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/2/code.py:14:#    The original task writes the transmitted complementary token directly onto the far endpoint\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D7/2/code.py:316:    Route complementary token shapes through the wire network, stacking them beside occupied targets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/24/code.py:48:#      sprites are pairwise disjoint; this avoids color conflicts while still allowing untouched\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D5/0/code.py:132:    - Each basin has a pair of special marker pixels (color 8), one on each side wall at the same row, defining that basin's target fill level.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/3/code.py:23:#     one whose contact mouth complements one hub edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/3/code.py:75:#     every sample, so humans can infer \"notch <-> protrusion complement\" from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/1/code.py:61:#   pair, preventing different-colored diagonal overlaps on background cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:99:    Each pair is horizontal and means [fill_color, marker_color].\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:216:    - In every pair, the left cell gives the target output color and the right cell gives the marker color to match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/20/code.py:49:#   lookup, so the key constraint is color-pair uniqueness and target-color uniqueness.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/20/code.py:363:    \"\"\"Pick pairwise distinct target colors disjoint from the source color set.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:3:# Name: 多色复合碎片+两阶段拼合\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:9:#    - 融合后的输入对象不再是“单色碎片”也不再是“颜色已经代表最终块”，而是：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:10:#      每个散落碎片自身就是一个 4 连通双色复合块，颜色分成外框色和内填色；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:11:#      同外框色的 2-3 个碎片先要在第一阶段拼成一个更大的子组件；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:15:#      D11 部分要求它先被切成两段同色碎片，例如上排 `[r r r]` 和下排 `[r r r]`。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:21:#      第一阶段的分组键来自碎片的外框色，而内填色只是随着该碎片一起搬运到第二阶段。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:26:#    - 每个最终子组件都切成 2-3 个碎片，且所有碎片面积都至少为 2，避免 D2 规则在 1x1 退化块上失效。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:28:#      又给中间 1 列空腔和上下 3 列空腔留出足够高度去拆成 2-3 段可见双色碎片。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:32:#    - 原题 `components_mask(g == col)` 默认“一个碎片只有一种颜色”；融合后改为\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:34:#    - 原 D11 假设“同色=同组”；融合后必须改成“同外框色=同组”，因为同组碎片内部还带着第二种颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:35:#    - 原 D2 可以依赖预对齐 frame；原 D11 则不能。融合后采用 D11 的更强设定：所有碎片都散落，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:37:#    - 第二阶段不能只按子组件支撑形状输出单色块；必须把第一阶段每个碎片携带的逐格 paint 一起带回终局，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:41:#      * 同外框色组恰有 2-3 个碎片；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:46:#    - 生成器先在终局矩形内构造 4 个最终子组件，再把每个子组件按连续行带切分成 2-3 个 4 连通碎片。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:48:#    - 所有散落碎片最终用 `random_free_location(..., padding=1, connectivity=8)` 投放到 13-15 的背景画布上，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:49:#      确保碎片之间不重叠且至少有 1 格切比雪夫间隔，因此 solver 的非背景 4 连通提取与真实碎片一一对应。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:53:#      * 同外框色的碎片重复出现，但它们还没组成最终大块；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:54:#      * 每个碎片内部都存在“外框色 + 内填色”的双色结构。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:55:#    - 输出里这些双色图样被原样带到终局矩形里，并且相同外框色的多个碎片会相邻组成一个更大的子组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:57:#    - 规则不依赖具体颜色编号大小；颜色只通过可见的“在同一碎片的外层/内层位置”参与推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:61:#    - 双色只发生在碎片内部，不再额外叠加独立标记层。行带切分使碎片纹理有秩序，不会产生密集锯齿噪声。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:64:#    - 没有隐藏颜色映射。内填色不是“被转换后才有意义”，而是碎片自身的一部分 payload。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/8/code.py:71:#   - 非背景 4 连通块就是单个双色碎片，不会被别的碎片粘连；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/24/code.py:9:#   - D18/2 把“框架+孔洞”改成“每个碎片都是一条整宽横条”，二维装配退化为按 y 顺序堆叠。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/24/code.py:17:#     破坏“每个条带对应一个碎片”。因此 generator 固定使用奇数高度，并让中心始终是一条独立中轴条带。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/24/code.py:22:#   - 原 solver 的 `_build_requirements()`、frame 搜索、2D 放置搜索都依赖“存在轮廓碎片”和“局部几何咬合”；\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:43:#       pair uses exactly one non-zero color and the generator enforces it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:63:#     - `main()` assumes exactly one valid training pair shares a color set.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:85:    - Match the training pair by identical non-zero color sets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:461:def build_dilate_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:478:def build_erode_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:495:def build_training_pair(kind: str, n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:497:        return build_dilate_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/0/code.py:499:        return build_erode_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:18:#    - D1 alone flips sprite lookup: src -> complement(src) sprite -> recolor to tgt.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:22:#         -> complement relation picks actual sprite color comp(mid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:27:#         complement rule says mid 1 uses sprite color 2\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:32:#    - The complement system is kept small and repeated: 1<->2, 3<->4, 6<->7.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:33:#    - Each sample uses exactly four mid colors: one full complement pair plus one singleton from each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:36:#      dst != complement(mid). That prevents the combo from collapsing back to either single variant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:44:#      semantic key is mid while the visible sprite color is complement(mid). Solver extraction is keyed by mid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:45:#      but searches for outside components colored complement(mid).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:56:#    - Because every sample contains a full complement pair among the mids and every query color is \"wrong\" for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:61:#    - Final recolor targets are drawn from {0,8,9} and kept separate from the six complement colors so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:66:#    - Every mid has exactly one outside complementary-color sprite bbox matching the placeholder size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:193:    Fill the frame with recolored sprites after decoding frame colors through a lookup table and then a complement rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:197:    - Outside the frame are complementary-color sprite templates, the usual overlapping 3x4 recolor legends keyed by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:203:    - Use the fixed complement relation on mid to choose the actual outside sprite color, then read the overlapping\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:205:    - Stamp that complementary-color sprite into each placeholder bbox and repaint its pixels to tgt.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:208:    comes from a chain: query color -> lookup legend -> intermediate color -> complement swap -> sprite template,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:250:        assert dst != sprite_col, f\"query color {dst} must differ from complementary sprite color {sprite_col}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:324:        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite candidate found for complementary color {sprite_col} of {mid_col}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:331:        assert len(sized) == 1, f\"expected one size-matched complementary sprite for {mid_col}, found {len(sized)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:341:                f\"extra sprite component for complementary color {sprite_col} is outside the base bbox\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:417:    \"\"\"Generate pairwise distinct sprite masks keyed by intermediate color.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:501:    \"\"\"Choose four intermediate colors with exactly one full complement pair present.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:517:      dst != mid and dst != complement(mid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/33/code.py:3:# Name: 多色碎片+上下对称+颜色交换\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/33/code.py:8:#    - 原题: 输入是单色散落碎片；solver 依赖左右镜像和同色不相邻，把它们直接拼回 LR 对称矩形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/33/code.py:10:#      1. 每个碎片先变成双色复合块。对任意 support 形状，按同一个 shape-only 规则推断“内填格”：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/33/code.py:16:#         外框色/内填色成对不同。solver 先从 frame 恢复 8 个槽位，再按双色碎片的 support\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/33/code.py:336:        pairs = {(int(p[\"border_color\"]), int(p[\"fill_color\"])) for p in pieces}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/33/code.py:385:      and the final transformation acts on mirror-paired fragments as a color payload swap rather than a second move.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/2/code.py:3:# Change: 六种规则之一: endpoints（取端点）、fill（填充间隙）、sym_fill（对称填充）、comp_checker（棋盘互补）、invert0（零与变量色互换）、sym（旋转/翻转） → 边界描绘\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/2/code.py:170:    - One frame interior is blank, two interiors form the training source/target pair with the same non-zero color set, and the remaining non-blank interior is the test source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/7/code.py:23:#      dock 最外沿挖出 4 格凹口模式，sprite 的接触带做互补凸起。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/7/code.py:26:#      的合法接触，所以 solver 必须逐组件验证几何互补，不能靠颜色，也不能靠取最大连通块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/7/code.py:57:#    - hub 四边外沿各有不同凹口，散落精灵上各有不同嘴型；输出中只有嘴型互补者被贴回。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/1/code.py:362:    forbidden_pair = _norm_pair(int(role_colors[_FORBIDDEN_ROLE_PAIR[0]]), int(role_colors[_FORBIDDEN_ROLE_PAIR[1]]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:24:#      a distractor. Old logic would pair blue/red by source-color or shape legends. The new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:3:# Change: 六种规则之一: endpoints（取端点）、fill（填充间隙）、sym_fill（对称填充）、comp_checker（棋盘互补）、invert0（零与变量色互换）、sym（旋转/翻转） → 连接线绘制\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:408:    - Match the training pair by their shared non-zero color set and treat the sparser member as the source pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:537:def build_endpoints_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:558:def build_comp_checker_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:581:def build_invert0_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:635:def build_sym_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random, idx: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:766:def build_connector_draw_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:849:def build_training_pair(kind: str, params: dict, n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:851:        return build_endpoints_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:853:        return build_connector_draw_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:855:        return build_comp_checker_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:857:        return build_invert0_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:859:        return build_sym_pair(n, colors, rng, params[\"idx\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D5/4/code.py:861:        return build_sym_fill_pair(n, colors, rng, params[\"keep0\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:28:#      4. 真 sprite 的接触端做成互补“嘴型”:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:35:#         的 dock 模式互补的那一个。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:37:#         任一 dock 模式形成合法互补，因此必须被几何约束排除。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:47:#      这样 2-4 个训练样例足以让人总结“凹口↔凸起互补”。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/35/code.py:71:#    - 输出里只有几何互补的那些 sprite 会回到对应 dock，颜色不会提供捷径。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/9/code.py:20:#     - Specialize those markers into a diagonal pair: exactly two same-colored cells sit at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/9/code.py:73:#     - At least one pair of matched sprites shares the same hole count but ends with different colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/9/code.py:75:#     - Distractors carry a diagonal pair in a non-legend color, showing that \"any marker\" is insufficient;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/9/code.py:216:    - If one diagonal pair is present and both marker cells share a legend color, repaint the whole sprite with that color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/9/code.py:219:    Key insight: The recoloring clue is the external diagonal marker pair; the legend only tells you which marker colors are meaningful.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/11/code.py:5:# Name: 拼成非矩形+无框架碎片\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:544:def build_sym_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random, idx: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:615:def build_training_pair(kind: str, params: dict, n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D19/2/code.py:618:    return build_sym_pair(n, colors, rng, params[\"idx\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/37/code.py:18:#   are repaired first using the D11 rule: compare local same-color support in each mirrored pair,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/37/code.py:114:    assert len(vertical_line_candidates) <= 1, \"paired vertical edge-line color must be unique when present\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/37/code.py:463:    - A few non-frame mirrored cell pairs inside the future rectangle may be damaged by isolated wrong colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/37/code.py:467:    - Repair the assembled rectangle by comparing each left-right mirrored pair: copy the side with stronger local same-color support, otherwise clear the pair to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/37/code.py:789:def _candidate_pairs(board: np.ndarray, frame_colors: set[int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/37/code.py:849:    candidates = _candidate_pairs(clean, frame_colors)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:3:# Name: 对称碎片同色+颜色交换\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:16:#    pre-output rectangle where each left-right mirror pair uses one shared color. Example:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:17:#    if the top pair is an L on the left and a mirrored L on the right, both arrive in color 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:20:#    The flow is therefore input pieces -> recover paired same-color families -> recolor families.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:22:#    If every pair got its own arbitrary color, the task would collapse into a trivial copy with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:24:#    The generator therefore uses four mirror-pair families but only three non-frame colors, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:37:#    complement of four mirrored hole families, so all non-frame pieces fit exactly in those holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:42:#    pairing rule directly. In the output, those same paired regions all change color according to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:48:#    pieces competing with the mirrored-pair story. Family colors are assigned with adjacency\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:55:#    pairing, not on an invisible ordering of coordinates or numeric color ids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:266:    Rebuild a mirror-paired rectangle from scattered fragments, then recolor each paired family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/7/code.py:276:    - After the paired same-color rectangle is reconstructed, apply the fixed non-frame color swap to obtain the final output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:22:#       Matching uses the complement within 0..3, so legend_actual_holes == 3 - sprite_actual_holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:46:#         complement key = 3 - 3 = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:64:#       No longer valid. main() must convert actual sprite holes with the complement map before recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:74:#       at least one class is absent, producing distractors that only erase under the complement rule;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:82:#     No ordering by color id, size, or position is used; only visible hole topology and the fixed complement rule matter.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:86:#     Distractors use the one actual-hole class whose complementary legend key is absent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:92:#     Legend keys are unique after complementing because legend visible hole counts are unique.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:128:    \"\"\"Map an actual hole count in 0..3 to its complementary lookup key.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:165:    Recolor grey frame sprites by matching the complement of their hole count to a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:176:    - Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase sprites whose complementary key is absent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:27:# e) Visual observability comes from repeated pair structure: two corridors, three marker colors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/10/code.py:521:    for color, tid, pair_idx in zip(marker_colors, chosen_template_ids, pair_assignments):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:53:    - Identify the example pair by matching border colors rather than matching interior palettes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:54:    - Infer the sprite-to-sprite transformation from that pair (reflection, color inversion, fill, endpoint extraction, checker complement, or symmetry fill).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:790:def build_fill_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:809:def build_endpoints_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:830:def build_comp_checker_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:854:def build_invert0_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:909:def build_sym_pair(n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random, idx: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:981:def build_training_pair(kind: str, params: dict, n: int, colors: list[int], rng: random.Random):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:984:        return build_fill_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:986:        return build_endpoints_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:988:        return build_comp_checker_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:990:        return build_invert0_pair(n, colors, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:992:        return build_sym_pair(n, colors, rng, params[\"idx\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4c7dc4dd/D2/0/code.py:994:        return build_sym_fill_pair(n, colors, rng, params[\"keep0\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/42/code.py:3:# Name: 颜色匹配+锚点碎片+两阶段拼合\n/home/lixinyu/sna