 D16 — 锚定碎片的特殊性 (meta)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D16/2/code.py:3:# Change: 恰好一块碎片包含标记缺失角对应的矩形顶点，该碎片作为锚定碎片优先放置在角落... → 多个候选锚定碎片\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:40:#         explicit pairing visualization layer after recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D6/2/code.py:267:    Key insight: The task still classifies sprites by topology, but the final answer also visualizes the pairing by extending a colored route from each matched sprite back to the legend that explains it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:4:#   → interior_cols 按碎片独立分配；每块碎片都有自己的局部颜色组合，不要求整块矩形共享同一组内部颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:8:#   输入仍然是若干矩形碎片和一个 3 像素 L 标记；输出仍然是把碎片平移回标记指示的矩形角。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:9:#   变化只在碎片内部配色：原题先生成整块矩形内部的 1-3 个全局 blob，再切成碎片，所以同一种 interior_col\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:10:#   往往跨多个碎片延续。这里改成先切碎，再给每块碎片独立生成 1-3 个局部 blob。共享边界上只保留少量同步的\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:15:#   仍限制每块最多 1-3 个局部颜色、总颜色池 3-5 个，避免颜色过多导致杂乱；同时要求多数相邻碎片的颜色集合不同，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:19:#   通常是单色最高频。D12 下各碎片可独立高填充、独立组合颜色，这个假设不再稳健。新 solver 不再硬编码最高频色，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:20:#   而是把所有出现过的碎片颜色当作候选 wildcard/border 色逐个尝试装配，按边缘频次排序以保持效率。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:21:#   其余装配逻辑仍成立：碎片仍是轴对齐矩形、不能旋转、外边框仍全是 rect_col、共享边只要求非 rect_col 位置相等。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:23:#   生成器先分割出矩形拼图，再在 assembled 坐标系里给每块上色，最后散落到背景上。标记先放置，碎片用\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:26:#   每块碎片都保留局部 blob，且相邻碎片常有不同颜色组合；共享边界的缝线很短，所以输出看起来是“边能对上、内部花纹\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D12/1/code.py:29:#   新 solver 假设真实 rect_col 至少是某个实际出现过的碎片颜色，并且用它做 wildcard 时存在唯一可装配矩形。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D4/1/code.py:201:    Key insight: the adjacent colored pair still teaches the color substitution, but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D14/1/code.py:185:    Key insight: The source-target pair still teaches the color substitution, but the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D2/1/code.py:266:    - For each framed pair, infer which source color is being transformed, which target color is produced,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/5/code.py:731:    for (_src, dst), tc in zip(colored_pairs, colored_targets):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/5/code.py:735:        (\"colored\", s, d, tc) for (s, d), tc in zip(colored_pairs, colored_targets)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5961cc34/D4/2/code.py:27:#   start colors remain the original red/yellow pair, which keeps color roles stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D10/0/code.py:30:# - Colors remain unique per rule pair, and bystanders never reuse a learned source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D10/0/code.py:135:    adjacent colored pair still names the source/target colors, and the nearby teal component\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/1/code.py:21:#      - odd hole-count difference inside a pair  -> each count keeps its own legend color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/1/code.py:22:#      - even hole-count difference inside a pair -> the two legend colors are swapped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/1/code.py:23:#    Example: a pair has (holes=1,color=red) and (holes=3,color=green). The gap is 2, so a 1-hole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/1/code.py:47:#    inter-pair gap is the structural cue that tells the human solver which two colors belong to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/1/code.py:157:    - For each pair, compare the two hole counts: odd difference means \"use each shape's own color\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D14/1/code.py:300:            pair.append((int(hole_count), int(colors[color_idx])))\n/home/li