ertical_line_candidates) <= 1, \"paired vertical edge-line color must be unique when present\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/0/code.py:587:def _place_sprite_pairs(out, inp, anchors, marker_colors, bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/0/code.py:620:    sprites = _place_sprite_pairs(out, inp, anchors, marker_colors, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/0/code.py:46:#    - 输出端虽然允许贴边，但仍保持对象之间的空隙；裁剪量被限制，避免只剩零散碎片。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D2/1/code.py:58:#    - Colors only encode sprite-anchor pairing. No ordering, remapping, or color-id arithmetic is introduced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D10/1/code.py:71:#      the training pairs visibly show that color matching is gone.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:535:def _place_sprite_pairs(out, inp, anchors, marker_colors, bg):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:584:    sprites = _place_sprite_pairs(out, inp, anchors, marker_colors, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D2/3/code.py:52:#   Colors only indicate anchor-marker pairing. No ordering, ranking, or arithmetic over color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:33:#      paired anchors and is replaced with `anchors_by_color[v] = [(r,c), ...]`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:55:#    - Same-color anchor pairs are few (1-3 colors), keeping the border readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:673:        pair = grouped_anchors[int(color)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:736:    pair = grouped[int(color)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D1/4/code.py:31:#    - 射线只走正交方向，不引入对角线碎片。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/0/code.py:56:#      few train pairs because the same three colors recur with repeated sprites across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/1/code.py:32:#     - pair each sprite to the anchor who